# MINI ERP + CRM — AI CODING RULES

## 1. PROJECT PURPOSE

This project is a small internal ERP + CRM operations portal for a wholesale/distribution company.

The application is used by: Admin, Sales, Warehouse, Accounts.

Do NOT add unnecessary enterprise architecture.
Do NOT add AI features, chatbots, fake analytics, or features not required by the PRD.

## 2. REQUIRED TECHNOLOGY

Backend: Node.js, TypeScript, Express.js, PostgreSQL, Prisma ORM, JWT, bcrypt, Zod, Puppeteer, dotenv, cors
Frontend: React, Vite, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, Axios, React Router, Lucide React, Framer Motion, Lenis
Deployment: Vercel (frontend), Render (backend), Neon (database)

DO NOT USE: AWS, Docker, GitHub Actions, Kubernetes, NestJS, Redux, GraphQL, Microservices

## 3. CODING STYLE

Code must look like it was written by a good final-year student developer.
Simple, readable, direct, easy to explain in an interview, properly typed.

Prefer: `const user = await prisma.user.findUnique(...)`
Do NOT create: factories, repositories, generic service wrappers, dependency injection systems.
Use normal Express controllers and services.

## 4. FILE SIZE

Keep files below 250 lines. Split logically if needed.

## 5. COMMENTS

Short and useful only. Good: `// Check stock before confirming challan`

## 6. NO PLACEHOLDER CODE

Never generate: TODO, FIXME, Coming soon, Dummy API responses, Placeholder functions.

## 7. BACKEND ARCHITECTURE

Route → Middleware → Controller → Service → Prisma → PostgreSQL
Controllers: request/response/status. Business logic in services.

## 8. API RESPONSE FORMAT

Success: `{ "success": true, "message": "...", "data": {...} }`
Error: `{ "success": false, "message": "...", "error": "ERROR_CODE" }`

## 9. HTTP STATUS CODES

200 GET/update, 201 create, 400 validation/business, 401 auth, 403 permissions, 404 not found, 409 conflict, 500 server error

## 10. VALIDATION

Use Zod for all POST and PUT/PATCH. Never trust frontend validation alone.

## 11. AUTHENTICATION

JWT with bcrypt. Never return password_hash. JWT payload: { id, role, email }.
Frontend sends: `Authorization: Bearer <token>`

## 12. ROLE BASED ACCESS

Admin: full access
Sales: customers, view inventory, create/edit/confirm challans
Warehouse: view inventory, add/remove stock, view confirmed challans
Accounts: view customers, view confirmed challans, export invoice PDF

## 13. DATABASE

PostgreSQL with Prisma. schema.prisma is source of truth. Use migrations. Never manually create conflicting SQL.

## 14. INVENTORY BUSINESS LOGIC

Never allow currentStock < 0. Every stock change creates StockMovement record.
IN: currentStock + quantity. OUT: currentStock - quantity (with pre-check).

## 15. CHALLAN BUSINESS LOGIC

Draft: does NOT reduce stock.
Confirmed: MUST reduce stock in a database transaction.
Cancelled: does not reduce stock.
Confirmed challan cannot be confirmed again. Confirmation uses Prisma transaction.

## 16. PRODUCT SNAPSHOT

Store productId, productName, sku, quantity, unitPrice, total inside challan items.
Historical challans must not change if product changes.

## 17. CHALLAN NUMBERS

Format: CH-2026-0001. Auto-generated. Unique.

## 18. UI DESIGN

Internal business software. NOT a generic AI-generated SaaS dashboard.
DO NOT use: excessive glassmorphism, glowing cards, neon gradients, huge hero sections, fake AI badges, unnecessary charts.

## 19. COLOR SYSTEM

#051F20 (sidebar), #0B2B26, #163832, #235347 (primary btn), #8EB69B (sage), #DAF1DE (light bg)
Only red for errors, amber for warnings, green for success.

## 20. ANIMATION

Framer Motion for page fade/slide, card entrance, modal entrance only. 150ms-300ms. Don't animate everything.

## 21. AI AGENT BEHAVIOR

Read .cursorrules, prd.md, tasks.md, schema.prisma before writing code.
Work ONE task at a time. Implement only the current task. Do NOT automatically implement future tasks.
Do NOT refactor unrelated files. Do NOT change the database schema without explaining why.

When uncertain between complex and simple architecture: choose SIMPLE WORKING ARCHITECTURE.
